## 9. International Production Readiness

| Category | Current Implementation | Confirmed Defects & Missing Features | Architectural Recommendation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Localization (i18n)** | Hardcoded English in all 558 files. | Zero i18n infrastructure. Cannot support multilingual deployment (Hindi, Punjabi, Spanish, French, etc.). | Install `next-intl` on Frontend and Admin. Extract UI strings into `messages/{locale}.json`. |
| **Currency** | Hardcoded Rupee (`₹`, `Rs.`, `INR`) in 39 UI files; `currency String @default("INR")`. | Hardcoded domestic currency prevents billing in USD, CAD, GBP, EUR, AUD. | Introduce multi-currency tables, exchange rate engine, and `Intl.NumberFormat` abstraction. |
| **Phone Validation** | Backend regex: `/^[6-9]\d{9}$/`. | Rejects any non-Indian phone number at registration and checkout. | Migrate to `google-libphonenumber` / `validator.isMobilePhone(val, 'any')` with E.164 formatting (`+1...`, `+44...`). |
| **Mapping & Geocoding** | Tied directly to `api.olamaps.io` (`OLA_MAPS_API_KEY`). | Ola Maps does not support geocoding or places outside India. | Implement a Provider Adapter pattern: `MapProviderService` with Google Maps / Mapbox for global traffic. |
| **Payment Gateways** | `RAZORPAY`, `PHONEPE`, `PAYTM`, `OFFLINE`. | Indian domestic payment processors only. International credit cards frequently fail on domestic Indian gateways. | Add `STRIPE` and `PAYPAL` to `PaymentGateway` enum and backend webhook processors. |
| **Payouts & Banking** | Requires `IFSC` code and `NEFT` method. | International vendors/artists cannot receive payouts via Indian domestic clearing networks. | Introduce IBAN, SWIFT/BIC, and Stripe Connect / Wise for cross-border payouts. |
| **Timezone Management** | Hardcoded `en-IN` date format in backend (`booking.service.js`); DB timestamps lack TZ. | Hardcoded IST formatting causes incorrect booking times for devotees and vendors abroad. | Store all timestamps as UTC (`@db.Timestamptz`). Format in the browser using the devotee's local timezone. |
| **Data Privacy & Compliance** | Single PostgreSQL instance with no data residency partitions. | Non-compliant with GDPR (Europe), CCPA (California), or DPDP Act (India) for cross-border data residency. | Establish clear data retention policies, user consent tracking, and localized cloud storage buckets. |

